  "review_families": {
    "closure": "Closure is restricted to exact-source reusable software-reference and dependency-review evidence for the current epoch. Fresh source-bound tests, actual assertion-killed mutants, observed restoration, and current analyzer captures must all pass before policy emission. Native PostgreSQL LOGIN/TLS/multi-backend contention, physical WAL power-loss recovery, authenticated Tailcat wire operation, deployment activation, and human promotion remain outside this engineering closure; they require the declared separate profiles.",
    "hash": "The reviewer recomputes each admitted file hash, all evidence reference hashes, and the raw external policy hash. The setuptools wheel is checked against the digest returned by its official versioned PyPI metadata. Hash equality proves byte identity; it does not authenticate an author's signing identity.",
    "identity": "Every native dependency surface is discovered by the original engine predicate and bound to exact path and SHA-256. Direct Python requirements and npm dependencies are exact pins matching the locks; all admitted Python registry origins are PyPI, all npm artifacts resolve under registry.npmjs.org. Build backend setuptools84.2.1 is separately inventoried.",
    "license": "The original native default HOLD for Psycopg is retained. A separately hashed, explicitly chosen inventory profile adds only the exact LGPL-3.0-only token after restricting it to psycopg3.3.7, psycopg-binary3.3.7, and psycopg-pool3.3.3. The unchanged native engine checks the complete installed Linux lock population; npm metadata is Apache-2.0 and setuptools is separately checked. No third-party distributions are shipped by the reference branch; no redistribution compatibility or legal opinion is asserted.",
    "organizational_standard": "The current branch must pass the fresh admission contract, complete candidate CROSS JOIN, exact JUnit binding, no-suppression rule, structural bounds, source/test refinement inventory, at least90% line and branch coverage, live coupled-service tests, and all twelve semantic mutations. Current compiler/static observations are independently required. Native review limits, protections, review family count, and static profile remain unchanged.",
    "provenance": "Source creation, upstream research, fixture repair, agent reviews, final executed witnesses, and native engine identity are preserved as hashed references. Old failure epochs remain historical observations. The supplied baseline and original native suite are not promoted or overwritten. There is no human signature, institutional attestation, or release approval represented by this automated engineering record.",
    "reputation": "First-party tools are new, session-authored engineering artifacts with no established external reputation. Their authorship and independent tool-boundary review are recorded; they receive no authority from reputation. Third-party dependencies come from the explicit PyPI/npm lock closure selected for the requested PostgreSQL references. Primary upstream API research, dependency necessity, exact identity, source review, and current executable evidence are assessed together. This assessment does not certify maintainers or give an unknown source implicit trust.",
    "source_integrity": "Current source is matched to fresh software and mutation receipts and rechecked after evidence assembly. Python lock artifacts carry SHA-256 and official artifact URLs; npm lock artifacts carry SHA-512 integrity. The fixture patch has an explicit upstream hash and changed-byte lineage; it is neither an upstream release nor native server qualification. No mutable revision, source rewrite, unknown origin, or shell=True launcher is admitted by this review.",
    "vulnerability": "A successful native pip-audit capture must cover every currently installed Linux locked dependency with exact version and no skipped or vulnerable record. The npm audit must cover the complete nine-package fixture lock with no reported vulnerability. The independently audited build backend is included. Platform-only packages remain outside this Linux execution claim, with exact false markers retained. Known-advisory absence is time- and feed-scoped, not proof of absence of vulnerabilities."
